# Prelude No. 2 in C minor, Well-Tempered Clavier II, BWV 871
# (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: a two-part invention in binary form, two halves, each
# repeated. A running sixteenth figure is passed between the hands
# against a walking bass in eighths; the second half opens with the
# figure turned upside down in E-flat, with little trilled turns.
# Serious but flowing, not heavy.
#
# Time signature and bars: 4/4, 28 bars, no upbeat; first half 1-12
# (to E-flat major), second half 13-28. The Mutopia score has both
# repeat signs, but its MIDI plays each half once (28 bars), so the
# repeats are written out below with play.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 92, with both repeats 224 beats, about 2:28. Track
# times (MusicBrainz track lists): Angela Hewitt (Hyperion, 1999) 2:29,
# about 90 with repeats; Rosalyn Tureck 2:14 and 2:18 (two sets), and
# Edwin Fischer 2:11, about 97 to 103 with repeats; Friedrich Gulda 1:39
# and Glenn Gould 1:26, which must leave out repeats or be very fast; I
# could not confirm which. 92 follows Hewitt.
#
# Structure (from the Mutopia score, checked against the MIDI; the keys
# are my reading):
#   1-4    C minor: the figure in the right hand over the bass in
#          eighths, then exchanged (2).
#   5-8    the hands chase in a sequence, two voices crossing; mordents.
#   9-12   toward E-flat major; cadence in E-flat at 12.
#   13-16  the figure inverted, E-flat major, trilled turns in both
#          hands.
#   17-22  F minor: the figure in sequence, a scale rising in eighths
#          in the left hand (21) over the dominant of F minor.
#   23-25  a falling sequence, one bar each.
#   26-28  back to C minor; final cadence.
#
# The performance (play, below):
#   bars  1-12  first half                bars 25-40  second half
#   bars 13-24  first half, repeated      bars 41-56  second half,
#                                                     repeated
# so the score's bar N is performed bar N (first time), N+12 (repeat)
# for the first half, and N+12, N+28 for the second half.
#
# Range: the bass notes below B2 (G2, F2, E-flat 2, C2) are lifted an
# octave, so the final low C sounds at C3.

tempo 92
play 1-12 1-12 13-28 13-28

voice mid 0          # two parts

dyn 1 mf             # first half, first time: the opening
dyn 5 mp             # score 5-8: the chase, lighter
dyn 9 mf             # score 9-12: toward E-flat
broaden 12 0.95      # the cadence in E-flat
dyn 13 mp            # first half repeated: an echo, a manual softer
dyn 17 p             # score 5-8, echoed
dyn 21 mp            # score 9-12, echoed
broaden 24 0.95      # the cadence in E-flat again

dyn 25 mf            # second half, first time: the inversion in E-flat
                     # and F minor
dyn 35 mp            # score 23-25: the falling sequence
dyn 38 f             # score 26-28: back to C minor, full
dyn 41 mp            # second half repeated: an echo
dyn 51 p             # score 23-25, echoed
dyn 54 mf            # score 26-28: the last close, firmer than the echo

rit 2 0.7            # the last two bars into the final chord
